  "caveats": [
    {
      "id": "industry_aggregate_not_logging_or_haul_cost",
      "text": "Total expenses are a NAICS 11331 establishment aggregate. They include administration, depreciation, overhead, non-logging activity and any in-forest log hauling performed by logging establishments; the table does not publish a logging-only or haul-only cost."
    },
    {
      "id": "double_counting_with_contract_and_haul_models",
      "text": "Do not add this aggregate to a separate truck-haul or silviculture cost without checking overlap. NAICS 11331 is the parent of 113311 and 113312; summing both child industries would double count. Payments from 113311 establishments to 113312 contractors may also appear in materials/supplies, creating intra-industry subcontract double counting at the parent level."
    },
    {
      "id": "survey_coverage_bias",
      "text": "The Annual Survey of Manufacturing and Logging Industries covers employer establishments. Non-employer contractors, owner-operators and community or informal harvest are not fully represented, while the harvest denominator includes all provincial harvest. This can bias CAD/m3 downward, especially in the territories."
    },
    {
      "id": "year_and_price_basis",
      "text": "Expenses are reference year 2024, the latest year in the 2025-12-18 table release, and are preliminary and subject to revision. Values are nominal 2024 CAD; no deflator or escalation is applied. The primary harvest denominator is the 2024 observed provincial harvest in provincial_allocation/119m.csv; the 119 Mm3 allocation column is a sensitivity, not the primary basis."
    },
    {
      "id": "component_detail",
      "text": "Only four expense components are published: total salaries and wages, materials and supplies, total energy/water utility/vehicle fuel, and an unpriced residual. Since reference year 2022 the energy, water and vehicle-fuel detail is no longer published. Shares use total expenses as the denominator."
    },
    {
      "id": "quality_symbols",
      "text": "Statistics Canada quality symbols are preserved: A/B/C/D/E are published estimates (D means acceptable, E use with caution), F is too unreliable, and x is suppressed. D is a data-quality flag, not a deletion. Suppressed or unavailable cells are blank, never zero-filled. Nunavut has a reported zero expense and zero harvest denominator, so its CAD/m3 is undefined and left blank."
    },
    {
      "id": "jurisdiction_aggregation",
      "text": "Only the 13 individual provinces and territories are used. Statistics Canada Atlantic Region and Prairie Region rows are aggregates and are excluded to avoid double counting. Canada is used only as national context."
    }
  ],
